arguments.report:
## Root cause

`FixedOffsetZone` (src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js) stored whatever it was given (`this.fixed = offset`) but its `isValid` getter was hard-coded to `return true;`. So `new FixedOffsetZone("CDT")` reported `isValid === true`. `DateTime`'s constructor (src/datetime.js:385) only produces `"unsupported zone"` when `!zone.isValid`, so with the bogus zone it fell through, computed `tsToObj(0, "CDT")` → `NaN` date, and returned invalid with reason `"invalid input"` instead.

## Fix (minimal, 1 file)

`src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js` — 2 lines changed:
- line 1: `import { formatOffset, signedOffset, isNumber } from "../impl/util.js";`
- `get isValid()` now `return isNumber(this.fixed);`

```diff
diff --git a/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js b/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js
index 364e065..3cffd6f 100644
--- a/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js
+++ b/src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-import { formatOffset, signedOffset } from "../impl/util.js";
+import { formatOffset, signedOffset, isNumber } from "../impl/util.js";
 import Zone from "../zone.js";
@@ -89,6 +89,6 @@ export default class FixedOffsetZone extends Zone {
   /** @override **/
   get isValid() {
-    return true;
+    return isNumber(this.fixed);
   }
 }
```

No other files were touched by me (the pre-existing dirty files src/datetime.js, src/duration.js, src/impl/util.js, src/interval.js were already modified before I started and are unrelated). No tests were modified or added.

## Verification

Bug-report repro (via `npx babel-node --only '/tmp,/luxon/src' --presets @babel/preset-env /tmp/bugrepro.js`, script in /tmp only):
```
zone.isValid: false
dt.isValid: false invalidReason: unsupported zone
```

